MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks felt like the strongest next choice because its live blues guitar and Muddy Waters and Howlin' Wolf material fit the blues interest reflected in my recent listening.",
    "The Rolling Stones collection and, if these are the albums I recognize, Revelator and Goin' Home connect with my interest in blues-influenced, guitar-driven music. Second Hand Heart also fits the roots side of my taste."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25, Earth Wind & Fire Greatest Hits, and the Mamas & the Papas collection do not match my current desire for blues and roots rock; broad musical familiarity is not enough to make me choose them.",
    "Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 and The Essentials give me too little evidence about the artists or music to judge whether they fit my interests. I would pass rather than assume they are relevant."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to assume that interest in established musicians means I want familiar hits across a wide range of sounds.",
    "Several compilations suggest that recognizable songs are enough to attract me, even though today I would rather explore a blues album than revisit a hits collection."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection that matters most to me right now is expressive blues guitar and roots-oriented music, rather than simply music from a similar era.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose immediately. I rarely act on recommendations, and today Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks is compelling enough to be my one choice."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my blues and roots interests but stretched them too broadly into familiar pop and greatest-hits collections."
}
